#: ../../../bash_to_xsh.rst:90
msgid ""
"Cause a failure after a non-zero return code of the *final* command in a "
"statement — this matches bash's ``set -e`` semantics where intermediate "
"failures inside ``&&``/``||`` chains are allowed. Xonsh will raise a "
"``subprocess.CalledProcessError``. Use ``$XONSH_SUBPROC_CMD_RAISE_ERROR = "
"True`` to additionally raise on *every* failing individual command."
msgstr ""

